"Oh my God, people are
gonna be like, it's crazy.

00:58:00.883 --> 00:58:02.858
"Everyone's gonna start getting canceled

00:58:02.858 --> 00:58:03.691
"or they're gonna be,

00:58:03.691 --> 00:58:05.796
"people are gonna put
Nicholas Cage in orgies."

00:58:05.796 --> 00:58:07.379
Although that's,

00:58:07.379 --> 00:58:08.386
that's not unrealistic.

00:58:08.386 --> 00:58:09.575
(everyone laughs)

00:58:09.575 --> 00:58:10.742
- Bad example.

00:58:12.158 --> 00:58:14.845
- I can't remember there being a case

00:58:14.845 --> 00:58:17.790
where someone got in trouble
for a Photoshop picture.

00:58:17.790 --> 00:58:19.607
Like, a big story.

00:58:19.607 --> 00:58:21.811
Like, because normally, you know,

00:58:21.811 --> 00:58:23.469
a picture at least, you know,

00:58:23.469 --> 00:58:24.671
there needs to be a lot more context

00:58:24.671 --> 00:58:26.958
behind why the picture exists

00:58:26.958 --> 00:58:28.994
and without reasonable context of

00:58:28.994 --> 00:58:30.820
why the picture would exist,

00:58:30.820 --> 00:58:32.622
people aren't really gonna believe it.

00:58:32.622 --> 00:58:34.657
I feel like it's probably
gonna be the same for a video.

00:58:34.657 --> 00:58:36.562
Like, if there's a video
of like, I don't know,

00:58:36.562 --> 00:58:38.967
like Robert Downey Jr. just like I said,

00:58:38.967 --> 00:58:41.513
like, punching a kid in
like a park or something,

00:58:41.513 --> 00:58:43.131
it's gonna be like, well,
one why is Robert Downey Jr.

00:58:43.131 --> 00:58:43.964
in a park?

00:58:43.964 --> 00:58:47.517
Why is he playing basketball
with a kid then punching him?

00:58:47.517 --> 00:58:49.058
The context is gonna be needed.

00:58:49.058 --> 00:58:50.403
Like, there's gonna be so many questions

00:58:50.403 --> 00:58:51.496
that are gonna need to be answered

00:58:51.496 --> 00:58:54.457
before you take a video seriously.

00:58:54.457 --> 00:58:57.320
- But, like, how long until
you do run into like that,

00:58:57.320 --> 00:58:59.424
you know, perfect
situation where it's like,

00:58:59.424 --> 00:59:02.603
oh, the story is there,
the narrative is there,

00:59:02.603 --> 00:59:04.050
everything lines up.

00:59:04.050 --> 00:59:06.175
The only difference is that
Robert Downey Jr. didn't

00:59:06.175 --> 00:59:07.367
actually punch the kid.

00:59:07.367 --> 00:59:09.804
But I can make him punch the kid.

00:59:09.804 --> 00:59:10.762
- It was a hoax.

00:59:10.762 --> 00:59:13.582
- I mean, fuckin' fake news
articles are bad enough already,

00:59:13.582 --> 00:59:15.980
you know, with how, you know,

00:59:15.980 --> 00:59:18.791
there are fucking
anti-vaxxers and flat earthers

00:59:18.791 --> 00:59:21.602
and just things that have been enabled

00:59:21.602 --> 00:59:23.274
because it's so easy
to stay in your bubble

00:59:23.274 --> 00:59:26.166
and really like strengthen
your own argument and your own-

00:59:26.166 --> 00:59:27.349
- It's a worrying time.

00:59:27.349 --> 00:59:28.182
I don't know.

00:59:28.182 --> 00:59:29.861
- It is definitely a worrying time.

00:59:29.861 --> 00:59:31.356
- But I don't let it get to me.

00:59:31.356 --> 00:59:33.698
I'm trying to enjoy life, you know.

00:59:33.698 --> 00:59:35.071
- I'm just trying to live my best life.

00:59:35.071 --> 00:59:37.529
- The world may be ending, but
I'm gonna have a good time.

00:59:37.529 --> 00:59:39.249
- I'ma still laugh at these memes.

00:59:39.249 --> 00:59:40.600
(everyone laughs)

00:59:40.600 --> 00:59:42.188
- I care about what I need to care about.

00:59:42.188 --> 00:59:43.021
No more.

00:59:43.021 --> 00:59:44.236
That's kinda how I like to do it.

00:59:44.236 --> 00:59:46.110
Like, I just think that
after a certain point

00:59:46.110 --> 00:59:47.679
if you just start
worrying about everything,

00:59:47.679 --> 00:59:48.924
you're just gonna be fucking miserable.

00:59:48.924 --> 00:59:50.804
And like, I think obviously, you know,

00:59:50.804 --> 00:59:52.028
when it comes to like, you know,

00:59:52.028 --> 00:59:54.353
you're voting on your politician,

00:59:54.353 --> 00:59:55.635
yeah, I think you should care about that

00:59:55.635 --> 00:59:56.468
and that should matter.

00:59:56.468 --> 00:59:59.950
But like beyond that, do
I care if a news presenter

00:59:59.950 --> 01:00:02.667
in the US says like
something fucking abhorrent?

01:00:02.667 --> 01:00:04.573
I'm like, no, honestly
it's not really my problem,

01:00:04.573 --> 01:00:05.660
and I don't really give a fuck.

01:00:05.660 --> 01:00:06.925
Like, maybe that's, I don't know.

01:00:06.925 --> 01:00:09.095
Is that, like, elitist to think that?

01:00:09.095 --> 01:00:10.050
- I think it's just-

01:00:10.050 --> 01:00:12.680
- Outside of my like, like,
you know, I don't know.

01:00:12.680 --> 01:00:14.865
To me like stuff that goes on
in the US sometimes I'm like,

01:00:14.865 --> 01:00:16.463
"That's honestly not my problem."

01:00:16.463 --> 01:00:17.693
Like, is that bad?

01:00:17.693 --> 01:00:21.063
Like, some people say
that's like a prejudice

01:00:21.063 --> 01:00:22.441
or ignorant mindset.

01:00:22.441 --> 01:00:23.885
Like, I have the luxury.

01:00:23.885 --> 01:00:26.179
- It depends on the context, right?

01:00:26.179 --> 01:00:28.416
Because the problem is that the problem

01:00:28.416 --> 01:00:30.010
with that argument I feel is

01:00:30.010 --> 01:00:32.412
that there's no way a human can care

01:00:32.412 --> 01:00:34.363
about absolutely everything.

01:00:34.363 --> 01:00:36.467
So, at some point you're
going to have to pick

01:00:36.467 --> 01:00:38.432
and choose what you care about.

01:00:38.432 --> 01:00:41.351
Otherwise, one, you're probably
gonna be a miserable fuck.

01:00:41.351 --> 01:00:42.903
And two, you're gonna wake up

01:00:42.903 --> 01:00:45.354
and you're just gonna be exhausted

01:00:45.354 --> 01:00:46.721
and not gonna be able to
do anything in the day

01:00:46.721 --> 01:00:48.683
because you just feel flooded.

01:00:48.683 --> 01:00:49.872
And I feel flooded enough

01:00:49.872 --> 01:00:52.734
with my own social media right now.

01:00:52.734 --> 01:00:54.505
And this is me, like,

01:00:54.505 --> 01:00:56.971
where social media is so
intertwined with our jobs.

01:00:56.971 --> 01:00:58.597
So, I see this stuff and I'm just like,

01:00:58.597 --> 01:00:59.748
I can't care about this.

01:00:59.748 --> 01:01:01.596
- I'm pretty sure that's how
people become nihilists, right?

01:01:01.596 --> 01:01:03.210
They're just like, they
look at the world as like,

01:01:03.210 --> 01:01:04.824
"Oh, the world is shit.

01:01:04.824 --> 01:01:06.313
"I guess nothing matters anymore."

01:01:06.313 --> 01:01:08.741
- I mean, it feels like it's
just been so much, like,

01:01:08.741 --> 01:01:10.993
heavier as well ever since
the pandemic as well.

01:01:10.993 --> 01:01:13.256
'Cause you're just trying
to like get by, you know?

01:01:13.256 --> 01:01:15.253
Life's already difficult enough
and then shit's going on,

01:01:15.253 --> 01:01:16.499
and you're like, fuck, man.

01:01:16.499 --> 01:01:18.650
Like, I'm literally
just trying to be happy

01:01:18.650 --> 01:01:20.321
for like 10 seconds here.

01:01:20.321 --> 01:01:21.154
Can I have this?

01:01:21.154 --> 01:01:23.236
- Yeah, I kind of feel a
bit jealous of our parents

01:01:23.236 --> 01:01:24.797
when they only had to care about the shit

01:01:24.797 --> 01:01:25.940
that was happening around them.

01:01:25.940 --> 01:01:27.376
Now I have to care about shit

01:01:27.376 --> 01:01:29.280
that's happening halfway across the world.

01:01:29.280 --> 01:01:30.858
- Like, when I see like, you know,

01:01:30.858 --> 01:01:32.107
my parents are gonna get fuckin' furious

01:01:32.107 --> 01:01:35.083
that they changed the bin
size of, like, the council

01:01:35.083 --> 01:01:36.888
by like 10% lower they're like,

01:01:36.888 --> 01:01:38.980
"Oh my God, this is unreasonable."

01:01:38.980 --> 01:01:39.813
You know?

01:01:39.813 --> 01:01:40.646
And like, I just miss the days

01:01:40.646 --> 01:01:43.155
where I could give a fuck
about stupid like that.

01:01:43.155 --> 01:01:46.436
Now I've got to worry
about like, literally like,

01:01:46.436 --> 01:01:48.256
cultural ending stuff.
- Shit that has nothing to do

01:01:48.256 --> 01:01:49.089
with you, right?

01:01:49.089 --> 01:01:50.291
- It's just like, I don't know, man.

01:01:50.291 --> 01:01:52.185
Like, I want to care about everything,

01:01:52.185 --> 01:01:53.065
and I want to give, like,

01:01:53.065 --> 01:01:54.997
people who are fighting
for like legitimate, like,

01:01:54.997 --> 01:01:56.147
good fights, I want to help them out.

01:01:56.147 --> 01:01:57.090
But at the same time, it's like,

01:01:57.090 --> 01:01:59.663
there's so much fucking shit going on.

01:01:59.663 --> 01:02:00.701
And obviously the internet's

01:02:00.701 --> 01:02:03.028
obviously made all the
information even more accessible,

01:02:03.028 --> 01:02:04.767
so there's so many more
things to care about.

01:02:04.767 --> 01:02:06.485
Like, all right checking
up on global warming.

01:02:06.485 --> 01:02:07.527
Don't waste too much food.

01:02:07.527 --> 01:02:08.387
What's going on over here?

01:02:08.387 --> 01:02:10.586
What's the, there's a civil
war going on in this country

01:02:10.586 --> 01:02:11.969
and like atrocities happening.

01:02:11.969 --> 01:02:14.997
How do I, like, legitimately,
like, give my energy-

01:02:14.997 --> 01:02:17.947
- You're literally just
explaining how to live.

01:02:17.947 --> 01:02:19.589
That's just life, isn't it?

01:02:19.589 --> 01:02:21.287
- Yeah, and like, I don't want to be like,

01:02:21.287 --> 01:02:22.608
"Global warming is more important

01:02:22.608 --> 01:02:23.962
"than people dying in this country."

01:02:23.962 --> 01:02:24.795
You know what I mean?

01:02:24.795 --> 01:02:27.255
Where do you draw the line
of where to start caring?

01:02:27.255 --> 01:02:29.108
- I mean, I think you can, like,

01:02:29.108 --> 01:02:30.807
pick and choose what you care about,

01:02:30.807 --> 01:02:33.085
but it's the difference
between being publicly open

01:02:33.085 --> 01:02:34.475
about that stuff, right?

01:02:34.475 --> 01:02:36.490
- I mean, I wouldn't say I
don't care about something

01:02:36.490 --> 01:02:38.740
as much or, like, oh my God,
this is so tough to talk about.

01:02:38.740 --> 01:02:39.573
- It is.

01:02:39.573 --> 01:02:40.781
- It makes you sound like an asshole

01:02:40.781 --> 01:02:42.918
if you say you don't
give a fuck about, like,

01:02:42.918 --> 01:02:45.813
Meilyne, what do you think?

01:02:45.813 --> 01:02:46.646
You're our manager.

01:02:46.646 --> 01:02:48.276
Will you make sure we don't get canceled?

01:02:48.276 --> 01:02:50.190
- Are we gonna get
canceled for this, Meilyne?

01:02:50.190 --> 01:02:51.023
But no, no.

01:02:51.023 --> 01:02:53.342
But no, I totally understand
because I feel like

01:02:53.342 --> 01:02:54.895
that's just part of being human.

01:02:54.895 --> 01:02:56.745
And you know, there's gonna be people

01:02:56.745 --> 01:02:58.158
that, you know, make the argument,

01:02:58.158 --> 01:02:59.414
well, you're privileged enough

01:02:59.414 --> 01:03:01.969
that you don't have to care about it.

01:03:01.969 --> 01:03:04.992
But, I would argue that surely,

01:03:04.992 --> 01:03:07.159
surely you also can't care

01:03:08.425 --> 01:03:10.609
about every single issue
happening in the world

01:03:10.609 --> 01:03:12.813
'cause you feel strongly
about this one issue

01:03:12.813 --> 01:03:15.013
because it definitely affects
you and I understand that,

01:03:15.013 --> 01:03:17.357
but surely that means that
you can't put the energy

01:03:17.357 --> 01:03:19.004
into caring about another issue.

01:03:19.004 --> 01:03:21.744
- I don't think there's any
person out there living any type

01:03:21.744 --> 01:03:25.168
of life, like, you know,
prejudice or not prejudice,

01:03:25.168 --> 01:03:26.372
privileged or not,

01:03:26.372 --> 01:03:29.158
who can deadass be in a
position where it's like,

01:03:29.158 --> 01:03:32.690
right now everything in the
world I need to worry about

01:03:32.690 --> 01:03:33.550
because it's important to me.

01:03:33.550 --> 01:03:35.005
Like, it doesn't matter who you are.

01:03:35.005 --> 01:03:36.773
Like, there's gonna be one piece of news

01:03:36.773 --> 01:03:38.951
where you're just like, "That
has nothing to do with me."

01:03:38.951 --> 01:03:40.115
- Something that resonates with you,

01:03:40.115 --> 01:03:41.995
that you like really believe in

01:03:41.995 --> 01:03:43.863
and that you fight
towards like helping that,

01:03:43.863 --> 01:03:45.408
like I'm down with that, man.

01:03:45.408 --> 01:03:46.241
- Yeah.

01:03:46.241 --> 01:03:47.301
At least you're fighting
towards something.

01:03:47.301 --> 01:03:49.008
That's better than someone just getting up

01:03:49.008 --> 01:03:49.841
in the morning being like,

01:03:49.841 --> 01:03:50.953
"I don't care about any of this shit."

01:03:50.953 --> 01:03:53.161
- Yeah, I mean, like, it's,

01:03:53.161 --> 01:03:54.802
it doesn't really bother me much

01:03:54.802 --> 01:03:57.434
when people get like
angry about, you know,

01:03:57.434 --> 01:03:58.592
"Oh my God, you don't care about this."

01:03:58.592 --> 01:03:59.787
But I hate people who are like,

01:03:59.787 --> 01:04:02.269
"You don't care enough
about this specific thing."

01:04:02.269 --> 01:04:04.587
Like, "You should be so
angry about this thing."

01:04:04.587 --> 01:04:07.216
And I'm like, man, I am
literally just trying to get by.

01:04:07.216 --> 01:04:09.606
- What dictates like the
quantitative worth of

01:04:09.606 --> 01:04:10.718
how much you care about something?

01:04:10.718 --> 01:04:12.259
- There's always some
people who are willing

01:04:12.259 --> 01:04:13.406
to get, like, outraged and, like,

01:04:13.406 --> 01:04:15.768
really light a fire up their
ass for something, you know?

01:04:15.768 --> 01:04:19.127
And like, you know, obviously
we need people like that.

01:04:19.127 --> 01:04:20.085
- Yeah, of course.

01:04:20.085 --> 01:04:21.408
- Otherwise shit doesn't get done.

01:04:21.408 --> 01:04:22.995
- You can't expect
everyone to be like that.

01:04:22.995 --> 01:04:24.000
- Yeah, but then I hate it

01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:25.934
when I see people, like,
blackmailing other people being

01:04:25.934 --> 01:04:27.417
like, "You should care more.

01:04:27.417 --> 01:04:28.540
"You should care so much more about this."

01:04:28.540 --> 01:04:30.392
- Because the problem with the argument is

01:04:30.392 --> 01:04:32.928
that there's no way to
frame it without the person

01:04:32.928 --> 01:04:36.522
who, you know, cares less about the topic.

01:04:36.522 --> 01:04:37.858
There's no way to frame the argument

01:04:37.858 --> 01:04:40.955
without making them, like, look good

01:04:40.955 --> 01:04:42.788
because it's just, okay,
you don't care about it.

01:04:42.788 --> 01:04:44.298
Therefore you are the asshole

01:04:44.298 --> 01:04:46.219
because you don't care
about this important issue.

01:04:46.219 --> 01:04:49.812
And I feel like, can we just
accept that we are all human?

01:04:49.812 --> 01:04:50.645
You know?

01:04:50.645 --> 01:04:52.781
We are all just trying to get by.

01:04:52.781 --> 01:04:54.249
Everyone has different issues.

01:04:54.249 --> 01:04:55.195
Some matter more than others,

01:04:55.195 --> 01:04:57.445
but it's a lack of empathy.

01:04:59.140 --> 01:05:01.018
You know, we,

01:05:01.018 --> 01:05:02.716
in order to empathize with your problem,

01:05:02.716 --> 01:05:05.758
you at least have to give us
some empathy as well, you know?

01:05:05.758 --> 01:05:06.591
And, I feel like

01:05:06.591 --> 01:05:10.357
there's just, like, a lack
of empathy in that sense

01:05:10.357 --> 01:05:11.425
in that kind of argument.

01:05:11.425 --> 01:05:13.587
- I'd like to think if I'm
being ignorant on any of this,

01:05:13.587 --> 01:05:15.581
that, you know, it won't result in fuckin'

01:05:15.581 --> 01:05:16.414
"let's cancel the boys"

01:05:16.414 --> 01:05:18.180
but just let me know down below.

01:05:18.180 --> 01:05:19.603
I will read the comments.

01:05:19.603 --> 01:05:21.517
So, if I am missing any big point here

01:05:21.517 --> 01:05:23.385
or I'm being ignorant,
please do let me know

01:05:23.385 --> 01:05:25.250
'cause I would like to change my mindset.

01:05:25.250 --> 01:05:27.213
- I don't think it's ignorance personally.

01:05:27.213 --> 01:05:29.701
I think it's just like being honest.

01:05:29.701 --> 01:05:30.925
- I mean, I'm exactly the same.

01:05:30.925 --> 01:05:35.283
I try to keep as open-minded
as possible about everything,

01:05:35.283 --> 01:05:37.961
and I've, you know, I've
definitely changed my viewpoints

01:05:37.961 --> 01:05:41.797
on certain topics thanks
to what people have said

01:05:41.797 --> 01:05:43.629
and what's been discussed.

01:05:43.629 --> 01:05:45.338
- There was one person who,

01:05:45.338 --> 01:05:48.202
'cause I think someone
tweeted at me and was like,

01:05:48.202 --> 01:05:50.192
"Connor, you shouldn't
say the word crackhead

01:05:50.192 --> 01:05:51.906
"as like a descriptive word.

01:05:51.906 --> 01:05:53.179
"It's a bad word."

01:05:53.179 --> 01:05:56.182
'Cause it apparently has to
do with a lot of, you know,

01:05:56.182 --> 01:05:59.756
like racial stereotyping back
in the war on drugs in America

01:05:59.756 --> 01:06:01.513
and stuff and it's used
as a derogatory term.

01:06:01.513 --> 01:06:02.433
So, I just stopped saying it.

01:06:02.433 --> 01:06:04.064
That was just 'cause someone
tweeted at me saying,

01:06:04.064 --> 01:06:04.897
"stop saying it."

01:06:04.897 --> 01:06:06.829
And I was like, well I
don't really need this word.

01:06:06.829 --> 01:06:09.192
Like, you know, 'cause I
said it a lot on the podcast,

01:06:09.192 --> 01:06:11.331
and you know, I realized
afterwards I'm like, yeah,

01:06:11.331 --> 01:06:15.295
I mean, there's like way
better ways to describe that,

01:06:15.295 --> 01:06:17.847
that feeling I was trying to
get across without using that.

01:06:17.847 --> 01:06:19.643
And I'm like, yeah, I don't
really need to use that word.

01:06:19.643 --> 01:06:21.894
I haven't said it since on
like podcast or anything.

01:06:21.894 --> 01:06:23.660
So, I'm like, oh, I haven't said it ever

01:06:23.660 --> 01:06:24.686
and I just don't feel the need to,

01:06:24.686 --> 01:06:26.566
and I'm like, cool, thanks for
letting me know, commenter.

01:06:26.566 --> 01:06:27.945
Like, if I have a bad habit, let me know.

01:06:27.945 --> 01:06:30.106
I'll try and get rid of it.

01:06:30.106 --> 01:06:31.153
If you're like, "Connor, you're fat."

01:06:31.153 --> 01:06:31.986
Fuck you.

01:06:31.986 --> 01:06:32.819
I'm working on it.

01:06:32.819 --> 01:06:35.532
(everyone laughs)

01:06:35.532 --> 01:06:36.827
Other things, okay.

01:06:36.827 --> 01:06:38.356
- The ones I hate the most are,

01:06:38.356 --> 01:06:40.564
"Connor, you got fatter."

01:06:40.564 --> 01:06:42.199
