there's less of a focus on sports,

01:15:39.751 --> 01:15:41.656
and more people are like
getting into, like, video games

01:15:41.656 --> 01:15:42.489
and stuff like that.

01:15:42.489 --> 01:15:46.016
Like, we literally talked
about how my nephew got bullied

01:15:46.016 --> 01:15:47.287
because he wanted to play sports

01:15:47.287 --> 01:15:48.428
but everyone was playing Fortnite.

01:15:48.428 --> 01:15:49.682
Whereas when I was growing up-

01:15:49.682 --> 01:15:51.102
- The other the way around.

01:15:51.102 --> 01:15:52.185
- It was the other way around.

01:15:52.185 --> 01:15:53.018
The cool kids were playing sport,

01:15:53.018 --> 01:15:56.632
and that's why sports had
such, like, so many eyes on it.

01:15:56.632 --> 01:16:00.709
And now I think because less
kids might be interested

01:16:00.709 --> 01:16:01.847
in sports, you know,

01:16:01.847 --> 01:16:04.306
you have to find a new way to
appeal to a younger audience.

01:16:04.306 --> 01:16:06.438
Otherwise they're just
not gonna give a shit

01:16:06.438 --> 01:16:07.471
at the end of the day.

01:16:07.471 --> 01:16:08.812
- This is gonna sound weird.

01:16:08.812 --> 01:16:11.534
But I think that video games are

01:16:11.534 --> 01:16:14.162
now more accessible than sports.

01:16:14.162 --> 01:16:14.995
- Yeah.

01:16:14.995 --> 01:16:17.021
- I think that's why they're doing better.

01:16:17.021 --> 01:16:19.595
Like, if you want to play a
game of rugby or football,

01:16:19.595 --> 01:16:20.553
you need what?

01:16:20.553 --> 01:16:22.489
Like, at least five a side.

01:16:22.489 --> 01:16:24.087
You need a lot of people to get that done.

01:16:24.087 --> 01:16:25.120
- And a lot of space.

01:16:25.120 --> 01:16:26.091
- Yeah, a lot of space.

01:16:26.091 --> 01:16:28.203
Like, anyone can play a video
game on their smartphone

01:16:28.203 --> 01:16:30.410
or whatever, and anyone
can download chess.

01:16:30.410 --> 01:16:31.618
- Anyone can play Madden.

01:16:31.618 --> 01:16:33.948
- Yeah, like, it's like, you
know, a lot of the sports,

01:16:33.948 --> 01:16:35.421
like I love swimming,

01:16:35.421 --> 01:16:38.755
but like finding a swimming
pool in Japan is so hard.

01:16:38.755 --> 01:16:40.504
- Yeah, without paying out the ass, right?

01:16:40.504 --> 01:16:41.917
- Yeah, and there's not
one anywhere near us.

01:16:41.917 --> 01:16:43.831
And like, I don't
fuckin' know where to go.

01:16:43.831 --> 01:16:46.187
- I mean, there's like
gyms that have them,

01:16:46.187 --> 01:16:49.328
but you have to pay, like, 150
bucks a month to access them.

01:16:49.328 --> 01:16:51.318
- Yeah, most sports that I liked as a kid,

01:16:51.318 --> 01:16:53.612
I realized how lucky I
was that there was like,

01:16:53.612 --> 01:16:55.797
in the UK you have so many
sports centers all around

01:16:55.797 --> 01:16:56.630
where you can do this,

01:16:56.630 --> 01:16:59.443
but now I'm like, it's
so hard to do the sports

01:16:59.443 --> 01:17:01.069
that I want to do and get into it.

01:17:01.069 --> 01:17:02.771
- I want to get back into sports.

01:17:02.771 --> 01:17:03.604
I don't know why.

01:17:03.604 --> 01:17:04.845
- And get like a newer
generation into them.

01:17:04.845 --> 01:17:06.589
'Cause it's like, I mean,
I'm not being funny.

01:17:06.589 --> 01:17:09.572
How are you gonna convince
a kid to go play golf

01:17:09.572 --> 01:17:11.372
when he can play Mario golf?

01:17:11.372 --> 01:17:12.700
It's so accessible.

01:17:12.700 --> 01:17:14.158
So easy.

01:17:14.158 --> 01:17:17.352
- And the problem is golf looks so boring.

01:17:17.352 --> 01:17:20.242
I'm sorry, but golf, like, I can not.

01:17:20.242 --> 01:17:21.882
There are some sports where I'm just like,

01:17:21.882 --> 01:17:24.022
I do not understand how
people can watch this

01:17:24.022 --> 01:17:24.983
and be entertained because,

01:17:24.983 --> 01:17:27.489
like, I've played golf before.

01:17:27.489 --> 01:17:31.712
'Cause like I used to like live
kind of near a driving range

01:17:31.712 --> 01:17:33.767
and it's just, so I had a period

01:17:33.767 --> 01:17:36.137
where I just really enjoyed playing golf.

01:17:36.137 --> 01:17:39.359
It was really satisfying
to like smack the ball.

01:17:39.359 --> 01:17:42.684
Wasn't rich enough to afford
my own golf clubs, so (laughs)

01:17:42.684 --> 01:17:43.823
- Another barrier to entry.

01:17:43.823 --> 01:17:44.781
- Yeah, exactly.

01:17:44.781 --> 01:17:45.770
That's my barrier to entry.

01:17:45.770 --> 01:17:47.410
But it's really fun to play golf.

01:17:47.410 --> 01:17:49.776
My God, it's so boring to watch!

01:17:49.776 --> 01:17:51.228
- I can not watch a golf game.

01:17:51.228 --> 01:17:52.556
- I mean, I'm sure the
people who are watching this

01:17:52.556 --> 01:17:55.205
who love watching golf, and
I'm sorry to disappoint.

01:17:55.205 --> 01:17:57.439
- But, like, there's so many
sports like that though.

01:17:57.439 --> 01:18:00.125
Like, I used to play tennis like a lot.

01:18:00.125 --> 01:18:03.007
But I can not sit down
and watch a tennis match.

01:18:03.007 --> 01:18:04.371
- Oh, I don't know, I can.

01:18:04.371 --> 01:18:06.821
- Some games are so good though.

01:18:06.821 --> 01:18:07.654
But they are long.

01:18:07.654 --> 01:18:08.487
They are long.

01:18:08.487 --> 01:18:09.320
- They are very long.

01:18:09.320 --> 01:18:11.265
- But I find it just so weird

01:18:11.265 --> 01:18:15.012
and interesting how, like, I
myself love playing the sport

01:18:15.012 --> 01:18:17.995
and yet I can't bear to sit
down and watch the sport.

01:18:17.995 --> 01:18:20.433
Like, you'd think if
someone played the sport,

01:18:20.433 --> 01:18:23.332
they would be just as
interested to watch it as well.

01:18:23.332 --> 01:18:24.415
- No, not always.

01:18:24.415 --> 01:18:26.572
Because the inverse is also true as well

01:18:26.572 --> 01:18:29.614
where I might, like, have no
interest in playing the sport,

01:18:29.614 --> 01:18:31.004
but I love watching it.

01:18:31.004 --> 01:18:31.962
- Oh yeah.

01:18:31.962 --> 01:18:33.254
That's more common I feel.
- Like, Garnt with League.

01:18:33.254 --> 01:18:34.529
- Yeah, like me with League.

01:18:34.529 --> 01:18:35.362
(everyone laughs)

01:18:35.362 --> 01:18:36.945
- Is that a sport?

01:18:36.945 --> 01:18:37.778
Ooh.

01:18:37.778 --> 01:18:38.611
- Ooh!

01:18:38.611 --> 01:18:40.646
But yeah, I mean, like
for example, I don't know.

01:18:40.646 --> 01:18:42.398
There's always gonna be,
like, massive sports,

01:18:42.398 --> 01:18:43.231
like football.

01:18:43.231 --> 01:18:44.314
- Oh yeah.

01:18:44.314 --> 01:18:45.413
- That's not gonna go away.

01:18:45.413 --> 01:18:46.934
That's, like, too deeply ingrained.

01:18:46.934 --> 01:18:51.361
But I feel like that's why the
Olympics are so weird to me.

01:18:51.361 --> 01:18:53.840
Because you end up watching
a load of these sports

01:18:53.840 --> 01:18:57.654
which you would in any other
circumstances have no interest

01:18:57.654 --> 01:18:59.560
in watching, but it's the Olympics.

01:18:59.560 --> 01:19:01.862
Does anyone want to watch
like men's volleyball?

01:19:01.862 --> 01:19:03.195
Anyone?

01:19:03.195 --> 01:19:05.060
- I never gave a shit about archery

01:19:05.060 --> 01:19:07.314
until I watch it in the Olympics.

01:19:07.314 --> 01:19:09.691
- There are a lot of
sports that are interesting

01:19:09.691 --> 01:19:11.649
when you have them or you experience them

01:19:11.649 --> 01:19:13.193
once every four years.

01:19:13.193 --> 01:19:16.418
And your country's kind of in the race.

01:19:16.418 --> 01:19:19.559
'Cause you gotta a horse
to root for, right?

01:19:19.559 --> 01:19:22.921
You know, I don't think
archery week by week

01:19:22.921 --> 01:19:25.075
Monday night archery, you know.

01:19:25.075 --> 01:19:27.301
You know, you gotta build storylines.

01:19:27.301 --> 01:19:28.685
You gotta build up characters.

01:19:28.685 --> 01:19:29.919
- The Olympics definitely opened my eyes

01:19:29.919 --> 01:19:32.274
to, like, some sports being really-

01:19:32.274 --> 01:19:33.107
- Like, handball.

01:19:33.107 --> 01:19:34.061
I never fuckin' saw handball before.

01:19:34.061 --> 01:19:35.269
- Oh my God, curling.

01:19:35.269 --> 01:19:36.868
I fucking love watching curling.

01:19:36.868 --> 01:19:37.701
- Curling is fun to watch.

01:19:37.701 --> 01:19:38.928
- I never thought I'd be into it.

01:19:38.928 --> 01:19:40.554
But I was like, you know what?

01:19:40.554 --> 01:19:42.419
This is hype as fuck.

01:19:42.419 --> 01:19:43.252
I don't know why.

01:19:43.252 --> 01:19:44.895
- Curling is like a Mario Party game

01:19:44.895 --> 01:19:46.814
that actually turned into a real sport.

01:19:46.814 --> 01:19:48.050
- It's like a mini game.

01:19:48.050 --> 01:19:49.950
But, like, every round is curling.

01:19:49.950 --> 01:19:51.209
- Literally, by accident.

01:19:51.209 --> 01:19:54.631
They're like, "Let's just
fucking make it real."

01:19:54.631 --> 01:19:55.948
- That's one sport I really want to play,

01:19:55.948 --> 01:19:56.781
like try out.

01:19:56.781 --> 01:19:58.367
Is there like a sport
that you've never done

01:19:58.367 --> 01:20:00.117
that you want to try?

01:20:01.490 --> 01:20:02.541
- Speed ice skating.

01:20:02.541 --> 01:20:03.958
It looks so cool.

01:20:05.124 --> 01:20:06.351
- That seems so dangerous.

01:20:06.351 --> 01:20:07.554
- I thought of that 'cause there was

01:20:07.554 --> 01:20:09.249
somebody who watches "Trash
Taste" reached out to me

01:20:09.249 --> 01:20:10.236
on Twitter, and I was like,

01:20:10.236 --> 01:20:12.272
'cause they were verified and
they had like 1,000 followers.

01:20:12.272 --> 01:20:13.443
And I'm like, what the fuck?

01:20:13.443 --> 01:20:14.332
And they were like-

01:20:14.332 --> 01:20:15.165
- [Joey] Sports?

01:20:15.165 --> 01:20:18.318
- Yeah, they were a pro
ice skater in like America?

01:20:18.318 --> 01:20:19.360
Canada?

01:20:19.360 --> 01:20:20.681
And they're like, "Yeah,
I love Trash Taste."

01:20:20.681 --> 01:20:21.772
And they were on the Olympic team.

01:20:21.772 --> 01:20:22.605
- Oh wow.

01:20:22.605 --> 01:20:23.438
- For like ice skating.

01:20:23.438 --> 01:20:24.271
And they watched us.

01:20:24.271 --> 01:20:27.181
I think ice skating is real cool.

01:20:27.181 --> 01:20:28.264
Real cool.

01:20:28.264 --> 01:20:29.347
Teach me.

01:20:29.347 --> 01:20:30.255
Nah, I love ice skating.

01:20:30.255 --> 01:20:31.663
I'd love to like go fast and do it.

01:20:31.663 --> 01:20:33.499
But that's too dangerous.

01:20:33.499 --> 01:20:34.528
- Yeah, it's dangerous as fuck.

01:20:34.528 --> 01:20:35.402
- I'd slam my face.

01:20:35.402 --> 01:20:37.422
- I'd have to, like, get
past that mental barrier

01:20:37.422 --> 01:20:39.442
of just like, you know when
you reach a certain speed

01:20:39.442 --> 01:20:41.619
and especially if you're not used to it

01:20:41.619 --> 01:20:43.284
you have to get past that
barrier of just like,

01:20:43.284 --> 01:20:44.727
"I'm going a bit too fast now.

01:20:44.727 --> 01:20:47.485
"If I fall, it's really gonna hurt."

01:20:47.485 --> 01:20:49.060
- You know what Olympic
sport I want to exist

01:20:49.060 --> 01:20:50.811
but will never exist is like,

01:20:50.811 --> 01:20:53.162
you know when you go
to like Round One here

01:20:53.162 --> 01:20:55.279
and you get the Zorb ball around you?

01:20:55.279 --> 01:20:56.112
- Oh yeah!

01:20:56.112 --> 01:20:58.303
- It's like football where
you're wearing, like,

01:20:58.303 --> 01:21:00.364
the balls where you can
just run into each other.

01:21:00.364 --> 01:21:03.178
That'd be such a fun Olympic sport.

01:21:03.178 --> 01:21:05.023
- Imagine just like 18 people on the field

01:21:05.023 --> 01:21:07.141
just fucking crashing into each other.

01:21:07.141 --> 01:21:09.389
- Honestly if you ever come
to Japan, come to Round One

01:21:09.389 --> 01:21:11.128
'cause most Round One have this.

01:21:11.128 --> 01:21:12.778
You're gonna see it on screen.

01:21:12.778 --> 01:21:13.810
- It's spo-cha, right?

01:21:13.810 --> 01:21:14.768
- It's spo-cha yeah.

01:21:14.768 --> 01:21:16.826
- So you're gonna see it on screen now.

01:21:16.826 --> 01:21:19.074
You can easily get access to this.

01:21:19.074 --> 01:21:20.109
- [Joey] Yeah, they're everywhere.

01:21:20.109 --> 01:21:21.526
- [Garnt] And then a lot
of Round Ones in Japan.

01:21:21.526 --> 01:21:23.149
- [Connor] They had like BB gun shooting.

01:21:23.149 --> 01:21:25.093
- [Garnt] Yeah, it's surprisingly.

01:21:25.093 --> 01:21:28.459
I remember when we did it
right in the fuckin' summer,

01:21:28.459 --> 01:21:30.423
which was a fuckin' stupid move.

01:21:30.423 --> 01:21:34.166
- Right after we had like
the biggest bowl of curry.

01:21:34.166 --> 01:21:36.218
We were like, we were
in the fuckin' Zorb ball

01:21:36.218 --> 01:21:37.166
just like rolling around.

01:21:37.166 --> 01:21:39.348
We're just like, "Oh, I'm gonna throw up."

01:21:39.348 --> 01:21:40.509
(everyone laughs)

01:21:40.509 --> 01:21:42.700
- It's surprisingly, it was surprisingly-

01:21:42.700 --> 01:21:43.533
- We should go back there.

01:21:43.533 --> 01:21:44.991
We haven't been there in so long.

01:21:44.991 --> 01:21:46.998
- It was surprisingly fucking
tiring to do that though.

01:21:46.998 --> 01:21:47.831
- Oh yeah, yeah.

01:21:47.831 --> 01:21:50.128
- It looks really light
to just run around.

01:21:50.128 --> 01:21:51.086
No, it's not.

01:21:51.086 --> 01:21:54.753
It is kinda like playing
a Mario Party game.

01:21:56.009 --> 01:21:57.552
'Cause like, it feels like,

01:21:57.552 --> 01:21:58.701
'cause you're playing football

01:21:58.701 --> 01:22:01.320
but it's got this like
really janky physics engine.

01:22:01.320 --> 01:22:02.696
(everyone laughs)

01:22:02.696 --> 01:22:04.924
It's like trying to drive
a car in like Cyberpunk.

01:22:04.924 --> 01:22:06.507
- Custom game mode.

01:22:07.377 --> 01:22:10.208
- Like, big head mode where
you're just fuckin' top heavy.

01:22:10.208 --> 01:22:11.930
- It's literally Gang Beast controls.

01:22:11.930 --> 01:22:14.763
(everyone laughs)

01:22:16.381 --> 01:22:17.762
- Yeah, fun as fuck.

01:22:17.762 --> 01:22:19.784
- I'd love that to be a sport.

01:22:19.784 --> 01:22:21.880
- Are you guys gonna go watch
any of the Olympic sports

01:22:21.880 --> 01:22:23.115
if it happens this year?

01:22:23.115 --> 01:22:24.323
- How the fuck do I apply?

01:22:24.323 --> 01:22:25.932
- Supposedly now that like,

01:22:25.932 --> 01:22:26.890
I think it's been confirmed

01:22:26.890 --> 01:22:29.171
that they're not gonna
bring any foreigners in.

01:22:29.171 --> 01:22:31.556
So, but, you can go see it at the stadium

01:22:31.556 --> 01:22:34.243
which means there's gonna
be way more available seats

01:22:34.243 --> 01:22:35.375
for the actual Olympics.

01:22:35.375 --> 01:22:37.531
I kind of want to do it just because like-

01:22:37.531 --> 01:22:38.693
- Do you know how to get tickets?

01:22:38.693 --> 01:22:39.536
- I'm gonna look into it.

01:22:39.536 --> 01:22:40.369
- I have no idea.

01:22:40.369 --> 01:22:41.749
- Because, like, if I can find it out,

01:22:41.749 --> 01:22:44.315
then I'd want to go just to say I've been.

01:22:44.315 --> 01:22:46.228
- Yeah, the only time I've
ever seen tickets available,

01:22:46.228 --> 01:22:48.259
the only way you could win
it was by buying something

01:22:48.259 --> 01:22:51.522
from Panasonic and you get
entered into a lottery.

01:22:51.522 --> 01:22:53.967
Which of maybe you'll
get the right to buy it.

01:22:53.967 --> 01:22:55.665
- Yeah, that sounds like a very Japanese-

01:22:55.665 --> 01:22:56.737
- That sounds like a Japanese thing to do.

01:22:56.737 --> 01:22:58.703
- I don't wanna buy Panasonic.

01:22:58.703 --> 01:23:01.490
I want a ticket to the Olympics.

01:23:01.490 --> 01:23:03.790
- Because this would be the second time

01:23:03.790 --> 01:23:06.670
that I've lived in a city
where the Olympics was held

01:23:06.670 --> 01:23:08.501
'cause I was there for London.

01:23:08.501 --> 01:23:09.592
- I wasn't there in London.

01:23:09.592 --> 01:23:10.425
- You weren't there in London?

01:23:10.425 --> 01:23:11.745
- I was in Wales at that time.

01:23:11.745 --> 01:23:13.667
- So, yeah, I was living
in London at the time.

01:23:13.667 --> 01:23:15.500
And yeah, I mean, I...

01:23:18.688 --> 01:23:20.676
During the normal Olympics
things just, like,

01:23:20.676 --> 01:23:21.784
get super, super busy,

01:23:21.784 --> 01:23:24.889
and I don't really like
crowds that much anyway.

01:23:24.889 --> 01:23:27.668
So, like, I didn't want to go
through the hassle of going

01:23:27.668 --> 01:23:28.805
to a sporting event.

01:23:28.805 --> 01:23:30.638
And I don't know.

01:23:30.638 --> 01:23:33.562
I didn't care enough about
the sport for me to want to go

01:23:33.562 --> 01:23:35.420
to this big sporting event where I,

01:23:35.420 --> 01:23:36.880
you know, I literally just said,

01:23:36.880 --> 01:23:38.255
the Olympics is where you watch sports

01:23:38.255 --> 01:23:39.335
you normally don't care about,

01:23:39.335 --> 01:23:42.507
but you watch it 'cause it's the Olympics.

01:23:42.507 --> 01:23:45.988
So, I don't even know what
sports I would want to watch.

01:23:45.988 --> 01:23:46.954
- I don't know, I feel like-

01:23:46.954 --> 01:23:48.121
- Would you just want to watch any sport?

01:23:48.121 --> 01:23:49.767
- But also, what if you watch a sport,

01:23:49.767 --> 01:23:52.057
but it's like a bad game,
like it's a bad matchup.

01:23:52.057 --> 01:23:52.890
It's like a stomp.

01:23:52.890 --> 01:23:55.853
It'd be like America versus
like Venezuela in basketball.

01:23:55.853 --> 01:23:57.943
Like, it's like, oh, come on.

01:23:57.943 --> 01:23:59.153
- Obviously Venezuela's gonna crush.

01:23:59.153 --> 01:24:00.736
- Obviously, obviously.

01:24:00.736 --> 01:24:02.008
- No, I feel like, I don't know.

01:24:02.008 --> 01:24:03.137
With those kinds of stuff,

01:24:03.137 --> 01:24:05.912
I feel it's just you go to
just enjoy the atmosphere,

01:24:05.912 --> 01:24:06.745
you know?

01:24:06.745 --> 01:24:07.578
'Cause like I remember-

01:24:07.578 --> 01:24:08.411
- How many have you been?

01:24:08.411 --> 01:24:09.883
- I've never been to the Olympics, but-

01:24:09.883 --> 01:24:10.960
- So, how would you know
the atmosphere's good?

01:24:10.960 --> 01:24:14.037
- Because, well, I mean every
other sporting event I've been

01:24:14.037 --> 01:24:15.552
to has been, 'cause, like,

01:24:15.552 --> 01:24:17.842
I remember I went to go watch, like-

01:24:17.842 --> 01:24:19.589
- But like Japanese
